tools.userPrompt:
Write a professional salary negotiation email:

Situation: {situation}
Current/Offered: {currentSalary}
Target: {targetSalary}
Role: {role}
{reasons ? 'Reasons: ' + reasons : ''}

The email should:
- Be professional and respectful
- Cite market data/experience
- Express enthusiasm for the role
- Make a clear ask
- Leave room for discussion

Provide 2 versions:
1. CONFIDENT (direct ask)
2. COLLABORATIVE (softer approach)

Write a resignation letter:

From: {name}
Company: {company}
Manager: {manager}
Last Day: {lastDay}
Reason: {reason}
Tone: {tone}

The letter should:
- Be professional and respectful
- Express gratitude
- Offer transition help
- Keep it to 1 page
- Include proper formatting (date, address, body, signature)

Write 3 different resume objectives for:

Role: {role}
Experience: {experience} years
Skills: {skills}
{goal}

Each should be 2-3 sentences, mention the target role, highlight key skills, and show career motivation.

Label: Option 1, Option 2, Option 3

Optimize the LinkedIn "{section}" for this person:

Role: {role}
Experience: {experience} years
Key skills: {skills}
Top achievements: {achievements}
Current text to improve (optional): {current}

Instructions:
- If {section} is "Full profile": provide HEADLINE (3 keyword-rich options, max 120 chars each), ABOUT (250-300 words, first-person storytelling, keyword-optimized), TOP 10 SKILLS to add, 5 sample EXPERIENCE bullets (with metrics), and 5 quick profile tips.
- Otherwise generate ONLY the requested "{section}", fully optimized, keyword-rich and ready to paste. For "Headline" give 3 options; for "About section" write 250-300 words; for "Key skills" list the top 15-20; for "Experience bullets" give 5-8 achievement bullets with metrics; for "Education" write a strong, keyword-aware education/credentials summary.
- If current text is provided, rewrite and improve it rather than starting over.
- Write in the same language the inputs are written in.

Write a cover letter:

From: {name}
Role: {role}
Company: {company}
Skills/Achievements: {skills}
Tone: {tone}

The letter should:
- Address the hiring manager
- Show knowledge of the company
- Connect skills to role requirements
- Include a specific achievement with metrics
- Be 3-4 paragraphs, under 400 words
- End with a strong call to action

Write a product description for:

Product: {product}
Features: {features}
Audience: {audience}
Tone: {tone}

Provide:
1. SHORT DESCRIPTION (50 words)
2. FULL DESCRIPTION (150 words)
3. BULLET POINTS (5 key selling points)
4. SEO TITLE
5. META DESCRIPTION

Write 5 bio options for:

Name: {name}
Role: {role}
Platform: {platform}
Style: {style}

Rules:
- Platform character limits (Instagram 150, Twitter 160, LinkedIn 2000)
- Include relevant emojis
- Add a CTA where appropriate
- Use line breaks for readability

Label: Option 1-5

Create 3 Google Ads for:

Product: {product}
Keywords: {keywords}
USP: {usp}

Each ad:
- 3 Headlines (30 chars each)
- 2 Descriptions (90 chars each)
- Display URL path
- Sitelink suggestions (4)

Focus on CTR and relevance.

Generate 15 email subject lines:

Purpose: {purpose}
Audience: {audience}
Style: {style}

Categories:
- CURIOSITY (5 lines)
- VALUE (5 lines)
- URGENCY (5 lines)

Rules: Under 50 chars each, no spam words, personalization where possible.

Generate 20 brand name ideas:

Industry: {industry}
Keywords: {keywords}
Style: {style}

For each name provide:
- Name
- Tagline (5 words)
- Domain suggestion (.com, .io, .ai)
- Why it works (1 sentence)

Mix: invented words, compound words, acronyms, metaphors.

Generate 15 slogans for:

Brand: {brand}
Description: {description}
Tone: {tone}

Categories:
- SHORT (3-5 words, 5 options)
- MEDIUM (6-8 words, 5 options)
- DESCRIPTIVE (9-12 words, 5 options)

Each should be memorable, unique, and brand-aligned.

Create a study plan:

Subjects: {subjects}
Timeline: {timeline}
Daily hours: {hours}
Goal: {goal}

Include:
- Daily schedule with specific topics
- Review sessions
- Practice test days
- Rest days
- Milestones and checkpoints
- Study techniques for each topic

Create mission and vision statements for:

Company: {company}
What we do: {does}
Values: {values}

Provide:
1. MISSION STATEMENT (3 options, 1-2 sentences each)
2. VISION STATEMENT (3 options)
3. CORE VALUES (5-7 with descriptions)
4. ELEVATOR PITCH (30 seconds)
5. TAGLINE (5 options)

Create 3 Facebook ad variations for:

Product: {product}
Audience: {audience}
Objective: {objective}

Each ad:
- Primary text (125 chars for mobile)
- Headline (40 chars)
- Description (30 chars)
- CTA button suggestion
- Hook idea for creative

Generate a SQL query for: {description}

Dialect: {dialect}
{tables ? 'Table structure:\n' + tables : ''}

Provide:
1. SQL QUERY (optimized)
2. EXPLANATION of each clause
3. INDEX RECOMMENDATIONS
4. ALTERNATIVE APPROACHES if applicable

Generate a README.md for:

Project: {projectName}
Description: {description}
Tech: {techStack}
Style: {sections}

Include: badges, features, installation, usage examples, API reference (if applicable), contributing guidelines, and license section.

Create an optimized daily schedule:

Tasks & meetings: {tasks}
Work hours: {workHours}
Top priority: {priority}

Provide:
1. OPTIMIZED TIME-BLOCKED SCHEDULE
2. PRIORITY RANKING of tasks
3. FOCUS TIME blocks for deep work
4. BREAK SCHEDULE
5. TIPS for staying on track

Generate LinkedIn headlines for:

Role: {role}
Skills/achievements: {skills}
Style: {style}

Provide:
1. TOP 5 HEADLINE OPTIONS (120 chars max each)
2. KEYWORD-OPTIMIZED VERSION
3. CREATIVE/UNIQUE VERSION
4. WHAT MAKES EACH EFFECTIVE
5. TIPS for headline optimization

Create a Twitter/X thread about: {topic}

Length: {length}
Style: {style}

Provide:
1. HOOK TWEET (attention-grabbing opener)
2. THREAD BODY (numbered tweets, each under 280 chars)
3. CLOSING CTA tweet
4. 3 ALTERNATIVE HOOK OPTIONS
5. BEST TIME TO POST

Write a poem about: {topic}

Style: {style}
Mood: {mood}

Provide:
1. POEM (in requested style)
2. TITLE
3. 2 ALTERNATIVE VERSIONS (different style/mood)
4. BRIEF ANALYSIS (themes, literary devices used)

Write captions for: {content}

Platform: {platform}
Vibe: {vibe}

Provide:
1. TOP 5 CAPTION OPTIONS
2. SHORT VERSION (under 50 chars)
3. LONG VERSION (with story/context)
4. HASHTAGS (15-20 relevant)
5. EMOJI SUGGESTIONS

Write a professional bio:

Name: {name}
Details: {details}
Purpose: {purpose}
Length: {length}

Provide:
1. PRIMARY BIO (requested length)
2. FIRST-PERSON VERSION
3. THIRD-PERSON VERSION
4. ONE-LINER VERSION
5. IMPROVEMENT SUGGESTIONS

Write a {emailType} email:

Details: {details}
Tone: {tone}

Provide:
1. SUBJECT LINE (3 options)
2. EMAIL BODY (ready to send)
3. ALTERNATIVE VERSION
4. FOLLOW-UP EMAIL (if no reply in 3 days)
5. KEY PHRASES for {emailType}
